.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt MALLOC 3
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm malloc
.Nm free
.Nm calloc
.Nm realloc
.Nm posix_memalign
.Nm aligned_alloc
.Nd allocate and free memory
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In stdlib.h
.Ft void *
.Fn malloc "size_t size"
.Ft void
.Fn free "void *pointer"
.Ft void *
.Fn calloc "size_t count" "size_t size"
.Ft void *
.Fn realloc "void *pointer" "size_t size"
.Ft int
.Fn posix_memalign "void **pointer" "size_t alignment" "size_t size"
.Ft void *
.Fn aligned_alloc "size_t alignment" "size_t size"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The allocator manages the process heap. The hardened backend is the default; a tiny backend
is available for constrained builds.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The allocating functions return a pointer or a null pointer. .Fn free returns no value.
.Fn posix_memalign returns 0 or an errno value.
.Sh ERRORS
.Er ENOMEM is returned when the request cannot be satisfied. .Er EINVAL is returned for an
invalid alignment.
.Sh STANDARDS
ISO C23 and POSIX.1-2024; ring 0.
.Sh CAVEATS
The hardened allocator is the default and supports MALLOC_OPTIONS and junk filling. The tiny
allocator is not part of the default libc.so.1. See C49 and document 08.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr malloc 3
.Xr libc 7
